body.text:
The remote mesh should transport evidence/work candidates, but unchanged or semantically equivalent messages must not repeatedly create current obligations. BonfyreQueue is already WorkGraph-backed and BonfyreGraph already has content-addressed operator/lineage concepts; use existing canonical identities rather than another dedup database.

Derive a stable semantic work-demand identity from message type + normalized predicate/target + relevant basis/evidence refs + validity scope, separate from transport event_id and Git commit SHA. On import:
- new transport event with an already-open equivalent demand attaches evidence/causal provenance to the existing WorkGraph obligation rather than duplicating it;
- an already-satisfied demand becomes historical evidence unless new basis/validity invalidates the prior solution;
- deterministic invalid envelope/content digest gets terminal quarantine until the remote content/address changes, not a refusal counter every sync;
- old Run8 coordination events stay evidence and are not replayed as fresh obligations merely because a new campaign starts;
- genuinely changed evidence/basis can re-open or derive a new obligation with an explicit edge.

Do not make BonfyreGraph the WorkGraph owner and do not make Git commit identity semantic identity. Prove idempotent import on one duplicate/equivalent event and legitimate reactivation on one changed-basis event.
